From 354f4a3fadca94fa5ee64b4a12bd00b152aaa8cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Son Nguyen <son.nguyen.xg@bp.renesas.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Jul 2025 11:53:21 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] linux-yocto: update kernel to support multiple features for
 RZ/V2H and RZ/G2L boards

This patch includes multiple enhancements and fixes for Renesas RZ boards,
particularly for RZ/V2H and RZ/G2L platforms. Changes are aimed at supporting
additional peripherals, fixing display issues, and enhancing kernel functionality.

Highlights:
- Fix screen flickering on RZ/G2L and RZ/V2L EVKs by updating DU driver, MIPI DSI, and DT.
- Enable I3C and RSPI communication on RZ/V2H EVK.
- Add GPIO dummy driver.
- Update USB3/PHY initialization for USB host controller.
- Resolve GPU init issue by type-correcting variable declaration in CPG driver.
- Add endpoint PCIe node and driver support.
- Add support for MIPI-CSI camera.
- Silence affinity warning for MSI IRQs in suspend mode.
- Enable USB Video Class support in defconfig.
- Improve clock handling in RSND driver to avoid atomic deadlocks.
- Add SYSC driver for system controller support.
- Support Renesas RSCI for I2C and SPI.
- Add PCIe device ID for endpoint test.
- Use GFP_DMA memory flag for endpoint test operations.
- Minor cleanup to align with kernel coding style.
- Add of_syscon_register_regmap() for non-MMIO syscon support.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Tien Nguyen <tien.nguyen.uh@renesas.com>
